<div class="unit-details">

    <!-- Overview & Objectives Split -->
    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="content-box">
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-binoculars"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">This unit takes you inside the computer to
                understand what actually makes it work. You will learn the roles of key hardware components, how
                devices communicate through networks, and why machines follow strict rules instead of "thinking"
                like humans. You will also explore Boolean logic — the true/false building blocks behind every
                decision a computer makes. You will use real-world examples, truth tables, and practical logic
                puzzles to understand what's happening inside a computer system and how simple rules drive all
                digital decision-making.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box">
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-bullseye"></i> Unit Objectives</h2>
            <ul class="custom-list">
                <li>Identify core hardware components (CPU, RAM, Storage, Input/Output) and explain their functions.</li>
                <li>Distinguish clearly between hardware and software.</li>
                <li>Understand how networks work (LAN, WAN, the Internet) and how devices share information.</li>
                <li>Explain why computers rely on Boolean logic and describe AND, OR, and NOT.</li>
                <li>Build and interpret truth tables.</li>
                <li>Apply logic to real scenarios using practical activities and logic-based problem solving.</li>
                <li>Combine multiple conditions to design a simple "smart" response system on paper or through a practical activity.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Concepts -->
    <div class="content-box">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Concepts</h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">This unit focuses on three SGS Computer Science concepts:</p>
        <div class="concepts-grid">
            <div class="concept-card">
                <h3 class="concept-name"><i class="fa-solid fa-shapes"></i> Form</h3>
                <p class="concept-def">Structure and organisation in systems.</p>
                <p class="concept-context"><strong>In this unit:</strong> Students map the structure of a
                    computer and identify how components form a functioning system.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="concept-card">
                <h3 class="concept-name"><i class="fa-solid fa-diagram-project"></i> Logic</h3>
                <p class="concept-def">Rules that govern decisions and outcomes.</p>
                <p class="concept-context"><strong>In this unit:</strong> Students use Boolean operations to
                    reason through puzzles, scenarios, and rule-based systems.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="concept-card">
                <h3 class="concept-name"><i class="fa-solid fa-rocket"></i> Innovation</h3>
                <p class="concept-def">Applying ideas to new or improved solutions.</p>
                <p class="concept-context"><strong>In this unit:</strong> Students design a simple "smart
                    system" using logical rules to solve a real problem.</p>
